### Concept & Implementation
A navigable 3D world in which the user can walk up to a wall and upload pictures. Each picture appears on the sides of a cube, and the cubes are arranged in a row of five on the wall. The project also attempted to implement a filter so that only cat photos would be accepted. Turning uploads into physical objects. Putting images on cubes in a walkable space makes a gallery of user content feel spatial and tangible. A playful constraint. Limiting uploads to cat photos adds humour and a clear theme, and it raises an interesting question about who decides what belongs in a shared space. The idea is fun, but image classification is not perfectly reliable, so some non-cats could slip through or real cats could be rejected. Making it clear to the user what happens when a photo is rejected would help. Some suggestions: Allow the cubes to be rotated, rearranged, or clicked for a close-up of each image. Add multiple walls or rooms, each with a different allowed subject. Show playful feedback when a non-cat image is rejected, so the filter becomes part of the experience.
